    "title": "pandas.DatetimeIndex.std — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DatetimeIndex.std#\n\n- \nDatetimeIndex.std(**args* ,***kwargs* )[source]#\n- Return sample standard deviation over requested axis. Normalized by N-1 by default. This can be changed using the ddof argument \n  - Parameters\n    - **axis** int optional, default None\n    - Axis for the function to be applied on. For Series this parameter is unused and defaults to None.\n    - **ddof** int, default 1\n    - Degrees of Freedom. The divisor used in calculations is N - ddof, where N represents the number of elements.\n    - **skipna** bool, default True\n    - Exclude NA/null values. If an entire row/column is NA, the result will be NA.\n  - Returns\n    - Timedelta",
    "markdown_length": 665,
